10:43:56 INFO ==== /pl/active/Leyk_Lab/data/HISDAC_US_V2/BUA_README.txt ====
These files are part of the dataset
"Historical built-up areas (BUA) - gridded surfaces for the U.S. from 1810 to 2020",
contained in the dataverse HISDAC-US: Historical Settlement Data Compilation for the United States 
(https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/hisdacus).

Reference:
Ahn, Y., Leyk, S., Uhl, J. H., & McShane, C. M. (2024). An Integrated Multi-Source Dataset for Measuring Settlement Evolution in the United States from 1810 to 2020. Scientific Data 2024 11:1, 11(1), 1�16. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-03081-x
https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/OPSSWR, Harvard Dataverse. 

Related Publication:
Leyk, Stefan; Uhl, Johannes H., 2018, "HISDAC-US: Historical Settlement Data Compilation for the Conterminous United States Over 200 Years," Scientific Data 5:180175
https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2018.175
Uhl, J. H. et al. Fine-grained, spatio-temporal datasets measuring 200 years of landdevelopment in the United States. Earth Syst. Sci. Data 96�114 (2020). doi:10.4324/9781315019444-13


The gridded surfaces (*.tif) contained in the BUA.tar.gz archive represent built-up areas (1) versus not built-up areas (0)
within grid cells of 250x250m, for each half-decade from 1810 to 2015. A grid cell is considered built-up if it contains at least one built-up property in a given year.

Abbreviations and explanations:
BUA:			Built-up areas. Grid cells containing at least one built-up property in a given year.

Data source: 
- Zillow Transaction and Assessment Dataset (ZTRAX) (c) Zillow Inc.
- Parcel (c) Parcel Atlas
- BuildZero Open City Model
Spatial resolution: 250m
Coordinate reference system:
USA Contiguous Albers Equal Area Conic USGS version (EPSG:5070)
https://spatialreference.org/ref/sr-org/usa_contiguous_albers_equal_area_conic_usgs_version-2/
Proj4: +proj=aea +lat_1=29.5 +lat_2=45.5 +lat_0=23.0 +lon_0=-96 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +ellps=GRS80 +datum=NAD83 +units=m +no_defs

Contact:
Stefan Leyk
Department of Geography
University of Colorado Boulder
GUGG 110, 260 UCB 
Boulder, CO 80309-0260, United States of America
stefan.leyk@colorado.edu
==== end BUA_README.txt ====
