10:43:56 INFO ==== /pl/active/Leyk_Lab/data/HISDAC_US_V2/LU_Count_README.txt ====
These files are part of the dataset
"Historical Land Use for the U.S. 1940-2015: Class Counts Version II",
contained in the dataverse  HISDAC-US: Historical Settlement Data Compilation for the United States  
(https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/hisdacus).

Reference:
Ahn, Y., Leyk, S., Uhl, J. H., & McShane, C. M. (2024). An Integrated Multi-Source Dataset for Measuring Settlement Evolution in the United States from 1810 to 2020. Scientific Data 2024 11:1, 11(1), 1–16. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-03081-x
https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/PRJBUF, Harvard Dataverse. 

Related Publication:
Mc Shane, Caitlin M.; Uhl, Johannes H.; Leyk, Stefan 2021, "Historical Land Use for the U.S. 1940-2015",
https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/LNBJIO, Harvard Dataverse

The gridded surfaces (*.tif) contained in the counts.tar.gz archive represent number of records within grid cells of 250x250m, for each of the eight
land use themes on an accumulative mid-decadal scale (i.e., 1940  means that values up to 1944 are summed up from 1810). 

Historical Land Use for the U.S. 1940-2015 (Class Counts)
Abbreviations and explanations:
Geo-Referenced:		Records are geo referenced if an explicit latitude and longitude is provided in ZTRAX, Building records from Open City Model and Parcel Atlas used the centroid points of the polygons.
Missing Grid-ID:	Records without an explicit latitude and longitude, which could not be grid-indexed.
.tar.gz 'A': 		Agriculture
.tar.gz 'C': 		Commercial
.tar.gz 'I': 		Industrial
.tar.gz 'RC': 		Recreational
.tar.gz 'RI': 		Residential-Income
.tar.gz 'RO': 		Residential-Owned
.tar.gz 'GV': 		Governmental
.tar.gz 'VL': 		VacantLand

Grid Cell Value:	The number of records with a land use description for the individual theme
				
Data source: 
- Zillow Transaction and Assessment Dataset (ZTRAX) (c) Zillow Inc.
- Parcel (c) Parcel Atlas
- BuildZero Open City Model
Spatial resolution: 250m
Coordinate reference system:
USA Contiguous Albers Equal Area Conic USGS version (EPSG:5070)
https://spatialreference.org/ref/sr-org/usa_contiguous_albers_equal_area_conic_usgs_version-2/
Proj4: +proj=aea +lat_1=29.5 +lat_2=45.5 +lat_0=23.0 +lon_0=-96 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +ellps=GRS80 +datum=NAD83 +units=m +no_defs

